body:
Related to godotengine/godot-proposals#432

Godot C# classes are concrete, so they cannot be mocked in unit tests. This generates interfaces for all Godot classes during mono glue generation. Classes automatically implement their interfaces, so you can mock them with NSubstitute.

Example:

```csharp
// Before: Cannot mock
public class Player {
    private Node2D _sprite;
    private Node2D _spriteChild;
}

// After: Can inject interface and mock
public class Player {
    private INode2D _sprite;
    private INode2D _spriteChild;

    public Player(INode2D sprite) {
        _sprite = sprite;
        _spriteChild = _sprite.GetNode<INode2D>("child");
    }
}

// Unit test
var spriteMock = Substitute.For<INode2D>();
var spriteChildMock = Substitute.For<INode2D>();
spriteMock.GetNode<INode2D>(Arg.Is<NodePath>(p => p == "child")).Returns(spriteChildMock);

var player = new Player(spriteMock);
```

Added `_generate_cs_interface()` and helpers to `bindings_generator.cpp`. Interfaces are generated alongside class files. Also added partial interfaces for generic methods (`INodeExtensions`, `IPackedSceneExtensions`).

Generated `INode2D.cs`:
```csharp
/// <summary>
/// <para>A 2D game object, with a transform (position, rotation, and scale).</para>
/// </summary>
public interface INode2D : ICanvasItem
{
    /// <summary>
    /// <para>Position, relative to the node's parent.</para>
    /// </summary>
    Vector2 Position { get; set; }

    // ... all other properties and methods
}
```

Generated `Node2D.cs` now implements the interface:
```csharp
public partial class Node2D : CanvasItem, INode2D
{
    public Vector2 Position
    {
        get { return GetPosition(); }
        set { SetPosition(value); }
    }

    // ...
}
```

Note: This creates interfaces like `ILogger` in the `Godot` namespace which may conflict with existing code. For example, `GodotIdeManager.cs` needed `private class GodotLogger : ILogger` changed to `private class GodotLogger : GodotTools.IdeMessaging.ILogger`.
